text:
There's only one way to end this. For context re: degrees etc, I'm in Australia.

I got diagnosed with bipolar in 2016, and the meds I was put on meant I could no longer finish my degree (it was in music performance, I had really bad hand tremors). I also can't drive, so that basically sank all of my job prospects. Haven't been able to get a proper job since.

Switched to some shiny new degree the uni had just made up, called Electronic Music. Didn't learn shit (also the degree itself was seriously mismanaged, but that's a story for another day). I graduate in about four weeks with a completely useless degree. 

&amp;#x200B;

&amp;#x200B;

 Job-wise, I thought maybe I could get a retail job if I volunteered at a charity shop first, but that was a complete trap. I've been working at that shop for 2+ years and I still can't get an interview. 

Working at the shop is boring at best, some days I get abused by paid staff, and there's no room to get promoted. I fucking hate it, so I probably shouldn't be trying to get into retail anyway.   


&amp;#x200B;

I graduate end of this year (no ceremony of course, thanks covid), and honestly? I hate m degree
